%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: quality enhancement of TE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: 'The primary goal of professionalizing teacher education is to:'
    Options:
    - Increase the number of teacher education institutions.
    - Establish teaching as a respected, standards-based profession.
    - Reduce the cost of teacher training.
    - Focus solely on theoretical knowledge.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: Which national framework provides the guiding principles for reforming
      teacher education curriculum in India?
    Options:
    - National Education Policy (NEP)
    - National Curriculum Framework (NCF)
    - National Curriculum Framework for Teacher Education (NCFTE)
    - Right to Education Act (RTE)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key strategy for enhancing the theory-practice connection is:'
    Options:
    - Eliminating the internship program.
    - Extending and enriching the school internship with proper mentorship.
    - Focusing only on university-based lectures.
    - Reducing the amount of practical work.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The statutory body responsible for setting norms and standards
      for teacher education programs in India is the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - UGC
    - NCTE
    - NAAC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The acronym "CPD" for teacher educators stands for:'
    Options:
    - Central Planning Department
    - Continuous Professional Development
    - Curriculum and Program Design
    - Certified Professional Diploma
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a characteristic of a quality-enhanced
      assessment system in teacher education?
    Options:
    - Reliance solely on final written examinations.
    - Use of portfolios, reflective journals, and practical demonstrations.
    - Subjective grading without criteria.
    - Avoiding any form of feedback.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "PCK" in teacher education stands for:'
    Options:
    - Primary Content Knowledge
    - Pedagogical Content Knowledge
    - Professional Curriculum Knowledge
    - Practical Classroom Kinetics
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The NAAC is primarily responsible for:'
    Options:
    - Recruiting teachers.
    - Developing school textbooks.
    - Assessing and accrediting higher education institutions, including TEIs.
    - Conducting board examinations.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major challenge in the professionalization of teacher education
      is:'
    Options:
    - The presence of too many high-quality TEIs.
    - The prevalence of sub-standard and commercially oriented TEIs.
    - Over-qualification of teacher educators.
    - Excessive focus on practical training.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The integration of ICT in teacher education aims to:'
    Options:
    - Replace teacher educators with computers.
    - Enhance the reach, quality, and innovation in training.
    - Focus only on teaching computer skills.
    - Increase the cost of teacher education.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'Stringent entry norms for teacher education programs are essential
      for:'
    Options:
    - Restricting the number of teachers.
    - Making the program easier.
    - Ensuring that candidates with the right aptitude and skills enter the profession.
    - Focusing only on academic scores.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of a "reflective practitioner" refers to a teacher
      who:'
    Options:
    - Blames students for failures.
    - Systematically analyzes their own practice to improve.
    - Follows the textbook without question.
    - Works in isolation from colleagues.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: Which initiative provides massive open online courses (MOOCs) for
      teacher professional development?
    Options:
    - DIKSHA
    - SWAYAM
    - e-Pathshala
    - NROER
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'School-University partnerships are crucial for:'
    Options:
    - Giving universities control over schools.
    - Replacing school-based teacher training.
    - Providing a real-world context for student-teachers and fostering mutual learning.
    - Isolating theory from practice.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: Quality enhancement in teacher education requires a shift from
      a focus on _____ to a focus on _____.
    Options:
    - practice; theory
    - inputs; learning outcomes and competencies
    - quality; quantity
    - students; teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: The National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 recommends a 4-year integrated
      _____ as the preferred mode for becoming a teacher.
    Options:
    - "B.Tech.\_B.Ed."
    - "B.A. /\_B.Sc.\_B.Ed."
    - Diploma in Education
    - M.Phil. in Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key element of faculty development is:'
    Options:
    - Isolating teacher educators from new research.
    - Encouraging engagement with research and publication.
    - Reducing their workload.
    - Focusing only on their teaching hours.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The use of "micro-teaching" in teacher education is primarily
      for:'
    Options:
    - Replacing the full internship.
    - Evaluating teacher educators.
    - Assessing only content knowledge.
    - Practicing and refining specific teaching skills in a controlled setting.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The DIKSHA portal is a national platform for:'
    Options:
    - School administration.
    - Teacher professional development and resources.
    - University admissions.
    - Financial management of TEIs.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A culture of quality is best fostered in TEIs through:'
    Options:
    - External pressure only.
    - Internal self-regulation and a commitment to continuous improvement.
    - Avoiding all forms of assessment.
    - Focusing only on infrastructure.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The term "accreditation" in teacher education refers to:'
    Options:
    - The process of granting a license to a teacher.
    - The recruitment process for teacher educators.
    - The final examination for student-teachers.
    - A formal recognition that an institution meets certain predetermined standards
      of quality.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a 21st-century skill that should be integrated
      into teacher education?
    Options:
    - Rote memorization
    - Critical thinking and problem-solving
    - Blind obedience
    - Isolation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A robust mentoring system for novice teachers is important for:'
    Options:
    - Increasing their workload.
    - Providing support and reducing early-career attrition.
    - Criticizing their performance.
    - Replacing pre-service education.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "I" in the acronym "ICT" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Instructional
    - International
    - Integrated
    - Information
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'Quality enhancement directly contributes to the professionalization
      of teaching by:'
    Options:
    - Lowering entry standards.
    - Ensuring that graduates are competent, reflective professionals.
    - Focusing only on theoretical aspects.
    - Eliminating practical training.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "E" in "NCFTE" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Elementary
    - Educational
    - Ethical
    - Environmental
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'An "Inquiry-Oriented" teacher education program emphasizes:'
    Options:
    - Passive reception of knowledge.
    - Developing the capacity to question and investigate educational practices.
    - Following prescribed methods without deviation.
    - Avoiding research.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "Right to Education Act (RTE)" impacts teacher education by:'
    Options:
    - Mandating specific teacher qualifications and training needs.
    - Abolishing the need for teacher training.
    - Focusing only on student rights.
    - Reducing the number of teachers required.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A "portfolio" in teacher education assessment typically includes:'
    Options:
    - Only the final degree certificate.
    - A collection of a student-teacher's work showcasing growth and competence.
    - A single test paper.
    - The teacher educator's notes.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate beneficiary of quality enhancement in teacher education
      is the:'
    Options:
    - Teacher Education Institution
    - School Principal
    - Student in the school classroom
    - Government
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "A" in "NAAC" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Assessment
    - Accreditation
    - Association
    - Authority
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major recommendation for improving teacher education is to phase
      out:'
    Options:
    - All pre-service programs.
    - The 1-year B.Ed. program in favor of longer, integrated programs.
    - The use of technology.
    - The internship component.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "C" in "NCTE" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Central
    - Council
    - Commission
    - College
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'Action research by teachers contributes to professionalization
      by:'
    Options:
    - Adding to their administrative burden.
    - Generating context-specific knowledge and improving their own practice.
    - Being irrelevant to classroom teaching.
    - Replacing all other forms of professional development.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "T" in "NCFTE" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Teaching
    - Training
    - Teacher
    - Technical
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key feature of a professionalized field is:'
    Options:
    - Lack of any regulatory body.
    - Low entry standards.
    - A strong code of ethics and self-regulation.
    - Isolation from research.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "N" in both "NCFTE" and "NCTE" stands for:'
    Options:
    - New
    - National
    - Northern
    - Noble
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'Quality enhancement requires teacher educators to be:'
    Options:
    - Passive transmitters of information.
    - Role models of lifelong learning and reflective practice.
    - Isolated from the school system.
    - Focused only on completing the syllabus.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "F" in "NCFTE" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Faculty
    - Federal
    - Foundation
    - Framework
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A significant barrier to quality enhancement is:'
    Options:
    - High motivation among teacher educators.
    - Inadequate funding and resources for TEIs.
    - An overabundance of qualified applicants.
    - Strong school-university partnerships.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "E" in "NCTE" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Elementary
    - Education
    - Ethical
    - Excellence
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The use of simulations in teacher education helps to:'
    Options:
    - Replace real classroom experience.
    - Increase student-teacher anxiety.
    - Provide a safe environment for practicing complex scenarios.
    - Focus only on theoretical models.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "C" in "CPD" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Certified
    - Continuous
    - Curriculum
    - Central
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A "growth mindset" in teacher education refers to the belief that:'
    Options:
    - Teaching abilities are fixed and cannot be improved.
    - Abilities can be developed through dedication and hard work.
    - Only some people are born to be teachers.
    - Reflection is unnecessary.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "P" in "PCK" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Primary
    - Practical
    - Professional
    - Pedagogical
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "K" in "PCK" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Kinesthetics
    - Knowledge
    - Key
    - Kit
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "D" in "CPD" stands for:'
    Options:
    - Diploma
    - Development
    - Department
    - Design
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "N" in "NAAC" stands for:'
    Options:
    - New
    - Noble
    - Northern
    - National
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The vision of a professionalized teacher education system is one
      that produces teachers who are:'
    Options:
    - Technicians following scripts.
    - Autonomous, reflective, and agentic professionals.
    - Dependent on external directives.
    - Isolated from the community.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: quality enhancement of TE
